     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 218 of 2009",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7040\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend chapter 218 of the laws of 2009 amending the tax law\nrelating to authorizing the county of Greene to impose an additional\nmortgage recording tax, in relation to extending the effectiveness\nthereof\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThe purpose of the bill is to extend provisions authorizing Greene\nCounty to impose an additional mortgage recording tax for two years.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends Section 2 of Chapter 218 of the laws of 2009, to\nextend the authorization of Greene County to enact a mortgage\nrecording tax of fifty cents for each one hundred dollars of mortgage\nvalue until December 1, 2018.\n\nSection 2: Provides for an effective date on the sixtieth day after it\nshall have become a law; and will expire and be deemed repealed on\nDecember 1, 2018.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Greene County Legislature has requested the introduction of this\nlegislation by Resolution No. 15-16 of 2016, adopted January 20, 2016.\nThis is a home rule request by the duly elected representatives of the\npeople of Greene County.\n\nGiven the rising costs of Medicaid, pension contributions, and health\ninsurance, among other expenses, along with the 2% property tax cap,\nthe County seeks continued authority to extend a mortgage recording\ntax at local option.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nChapter 222 of the Laws of 2014.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect Immediately.\n",
